From 3dc66153d278eccb8af9d4d44835738d50d5ccde Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 21:38:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] add aarch64_ilp32 port

AArch64 ILP32 (-mabi=ilp32) on the arm64 ILP32 kernel ABI: the generic
syscall table with the 32-bit variants and the time32 calls, served by
the AArch32 (compat) handlers.

- 64-bit syscall arguments are register pairs starting with an even
  register (as arm): __SYSCALL_LL_E/_O, SYSCALL_FADVISE_6_ARG,
  sync_file_range2, mmap2 in 4k units
- struct stat64 of the kernel has the AArch32 layout (kstat.h from arm);
  stat uses statx first
- fcntl locks use F_GETLK64 (12-14), compat IPC with IPC_64 and a 16-bit
  ipc mode (SYSCALL_IPC_BROKEN_MODE), the ipc structs of arm
- types as x32: _Addr int, _Int64/_Reg long long; time_t is 64-bit,
  no _REDIR_TIME64 since there are no older binaries
- sigcontext/mcontext, jmp_buf and user regs keep 64-bit registers;
  ucontext is laid out as the kernel ilp32_ucontext (mcontext at 160)
- the TCB is two 32-bit pointers: GAP_ABOVE_TP 8
- vDSO LINUX_4.12: __kernel_clock_gettime64, __kernel_clock_gettime
- P32 relocations; the dynamic linker is ld-musl-aarch64[_be]_ilp32.so.1,
  the name GCC uses
- assembly zero-extends pointer and size arguments (upper halves are
  undefined in the ILP32 ABI); sigsetjmp keeps x19/x30 after the saved
  signal mask, which starts at 180; tlsdesc uses 32-bit words; memcpy
  and memset wrap the aarch64 versions
---
